From 9f29d1ecd207ed44f17af631780c0031563af557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:49:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Stop reconnect retries that cannot succeed and keep
 reconnect available

An automatic reconnect can reuse a delegate whose password prompt has
already been dismissed. Treating its dropped response like an ordinary
transport failure repeats attempts that cannot succeed without user
interaction and leaves the workspace without a useful reconnect action.

Carry explicit prompt-unavailable and user-cancelled outcomes through
askpass, SSH and the shared connection pool. Stop the reconnect loop for
those outcomes and verified OpenSSH authentication failures, while keeping
the existing retry schedule for transient transport and proxy failures.
Match the complete authentication-method list so a parenthesized OS
permission error is not mistaken for failed SSH authentication.

Notify the project when remote state changes and retain the actual
disconnect reason. Restore the existing disconnected overlay after a
cancelled or failed manual attempt only if its original workspace is still
displayed and disconnected. A successful workspace replacement must not
reopen an overlay on the obsolete workspace or steal focus.

Keep legacy askpass cancellation ordered after its response channel is
closed, so ending a remote Git operation rejects late replies without
leaving a detached adapter waiting for input. Preserve normal successful
password handoff and cancellation notification ordering as well.
